 ("RSHE-S-OSA-8", ("secondary","Online safety and awareness"), 8, "FULL",
  "ks4-18-radicalisation-misogyny; ks4-29-did-not-go-looking",
  "ks4-18 teaches the pipeline that carries misogynistic content. ks4-29 teaches the violence half: a violent video arriving in a feed is the first card in the sort, knife supply is taught at s17 as a website that is not a loophole, and s21 'Stop it, report it, say it' gives the routes, in the app, Report Harmful Content from thirteen, and a named person. s9 'What it does to look' teaches the distorted picture clause: repetition makes a serious thing look more ordinary than it is, which matters most for whoever is already struggling.",
  "Closed by migration 315. Where to go for advice about something seen online is now taught at secondary as three moves in order, with the reporting chain app first, then Report Harmful Content, and a person for the half a report never does."),
 ("RSHE-S-OSA-9", ("secondary","Online safety and awareness"), 9, "FULL",
  "ks3-27-when-it-turns-on-you",
  "ks3-27 s6 'Why it gets bigger online' teaches escalation as structural: three brakes a room has and a screen lacks, the face, the privacy and the forgetting. s10 'Three brakes that are missing' is the diagram. s8 'The quiet majority is the whole audience' teaches why one message breaks a pile on. s16 'What actually ends it' gives name it, save it, say it, and s18 'Where to take it' gives the routes in the app, in school and outside, with Childline's number.",
  "Closed by migration 313. Avoiding escalation is taught as a bystander move a fourteen year old will actually make: one message in the chat, one private message to the person, one adult."),
 ("RSHE-S-OSA-10", ("secondary","Online safety and awareness"), 10, "FULL",
  "ks3-27-when-it-turns-on-you",
  "ks3-27 s12 'Four things with real names' defines bullying, harassment, stalking and coercive control with the line on each. s13 checks that one rude comment is not harassment and a two sided row is not bullying. s14 is a five message scenario of coercive control, each message innocent alone, and s15 names the pattern. s16 'Where a name becomes the law' states that harassment, stalking and coercive control are criminal offences.",
  "Closed by migration 313. The name it sheet has every pupil write who precisely they would say it to, by role or by name, because vagueness there is the commonest reason nothing happens."),
 ("RSHE-S-OSA-11", ("secondary","Online safety and awareness"), 11, "FULL",
  "ks3-14-bodies-image-pressure",
  "ks3-14 names it calmly: 'One more kind of made content needs naming, calmly and briefly: pornography.' It teaches that made content including pornography is not a guide to real bodies or real relationships, that seeing it is not unusual and not a punishable thing, and carries a sourced figure on average age of first exposure.",
  "Closed by migration 309. The module now teaches the half that reaches other people: watching a lot of it can change what someone expects of a partner, and the damage is that expectation travelling into a real relationship."),
